            <ArticleTitle>Unusual cause of abdominal pain: pelvic vein thrombosis in a nonpregnant woman.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>254-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of isolated pelvic vein thrombosis in which clinical diagnosis was difficult and the results of routine diagnostic tests were normal. We eventually used ventilation-perfusion scanning and abdominal computed tomography to make the correct diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
